ve Thomas.","title":"Bob and Doug McKenzie"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Although created originally as filler to both satisfy and mock network Canadian content demands, the duo became a pop culture phenomenon in both Canada and the United States.","title":"Bob and Doug McKenzie"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Dave Thomas Comedy Show (later simply Dave Thomas) was a sketch-based, half-hour, five-week summer replacement series, which aired on CBS in the summer of 1990.","title":"The Dave Thomas Comedy Show"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The show starred Canadian comedian Dave Thomas, who is best known for an earlier sketch comedy series, "SCTV".","title":"The Dave Thomas Comedy Show"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Thomas himself served as head writer, while the writing staff included Hollywood scriptwriter Ed Solomon and Mike Myers.","title":"The Dave Thomas Comedy Show"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The series debuted May 28, 1990.","title":"The Dave Thomas Comedy Show"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Strange Brew (also known as The Adventures of Bob & Doug McKenzie: Strange Brew) is a 1983 Canadian comedy film starring the popular "SCTV" characters Bob and Doug McKenzie, portrayed by Dave Thomas and Rick Moranis, who also served as co-directors.","title":"Strange Brew"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Co-stars include Max von Sydow, Paul Dooley, Lynne Griffin and Angus MacInnes.","title":"Strange Brew"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Great White North (sketch) and The Great White North (album)
